=== Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Arith/MajorityVote.lean — 12 doc comment(s), 1 with a word
  l.174 ['assum']
    decl: theorem ae_eq_measurable_of_majority {Ω I K : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {μ : Measure Ω} [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
    doc : **FS131-E8-SI5C — majority decoding.** A `G` with values in a countable type that every `c x` equals unless an event `E x` of probability at most `p < 1/2` occurs, the `E x` pairwise independent over an infinite index set, is almost surely equal to a function measurable for the σ-algebra the `c x` generate. Neither `G` nor the `c x` is assumed measurable (the entry's finite-valued measurable variables are an instance).
